":128,"ds":"Piazzale Roma (Venetian: Piasal Roma) is a square in Venice, Italy, at the entrance of the city, at the end of the Ponte della Libertà, a road bridge. The bridge connects the islands that form the historical centre of the city of Venice to the mainland part of the city.","wpu":"Piazzale Roma","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Piazzale_Roma.JPG/960px-Piazzale_Roma.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Giardini Papadopoli","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.438511,"lo":12.320678,"d":292,"ds":"Giardino Papadopoli is a terraced garden filled with shade trees in the Venetian sestiere of Santa Croce, between the Venezia Santa Lucia train station and Piazzale Roma.","wpu":"Giardini Papadopoli","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Giardini_Papadopoli_-_Rio_Novo.jpg/960px-Giardini_Papadopoli_-_Rio_Novo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Santa Maria Maggiore, Venice","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.435,"lo":12.3169,"d":333,"ds":"Santa Maria Maggiore is a former Catholic church, now deconsecrated, in the sestiere of Santa Croce, Venice. The church, which was completed at the start of the 16th century, as part of a convent, was suppressed and deconsecrated during the decade of the Napoleonic Kingdom of Italy. It has since has been used as a stable, and a tobacco warehouse, before forming part of the Santa Maria Maggiore prison.","wpu":"Santa Maria Maggiore, Venice","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Chiesa_di_Santa_Maria_Maggiore_Venezia.jpg/960px-Chiesa_di_Santa_Maria_Maggiore_Venezia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tolentini, Venice","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.4374,"lo":12.3221,"d":403,"ds":"The Chiesa di San Nicolò da Tolentino, commonly known as the Tolentini, is a church in the sestiere of Santa Croce in Venice, northern Italy. It lies in a Campo of the same name and along the Rio dei Tolentini, near the Giardino Papadopoli.","wpu":"Tolentini, Venice","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Chiesa_di_San_Nicola_da_Tolentino_%28Venice%29.jpg/960px-Chiesa_di_San_Nicola_da_Tolentino_%28Venice%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ponte degli Scalzi","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.441111,"lo":12.3225,"d":551,"ds":"The Ponte degli Scalzi (or Ponte dei Scalsi, in Venetian; literally, \"bridge of the barefoot [monks]\"), is one of only four bridges in Venice to span the Grand Canal. The bridge connects the sestieri of Santa Croce and Cannaregio. On the north side, Cannaregio, are the Chiesa degli Scalzi (Church of the Barefoot or Discalced Monks) and the Santa Lucia (Ferrovia) railway station.","wpu":"Ponte degli Scalzi","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Ponte_degli_Scalzi_-_Venice_-_2016_%282%29.jpg/960px-Ponte_degli_Scalzi_-_Venice_-_2016_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Palazzo Ariani","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.4331,"lo":12.3193,"d":573,"ds":"Palazzo Ariani, also known as Palazzo Ariani Minotto Cicogna (in Venetian, Palazzo Arian), is a palace in Venice, located in the Dorsoduro district, almost opposite to the church of Angelo San Raffaele and not far from San Sebastiano. The nearby bridge Ponte del Soccorso connects it to the Palazzo Zenobio.","wpu":"Palazzo Ariani","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Palazzo_Ariani_%28Venice%29.jpg/960px-Palazzo_Ariani_%28Venice%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Palazzo Giustinian (Dorsoduro)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.4345,"lo":12.3266,"d":844,"ds":"Palazzo Giustinian is a palace in Venice, northern Italy, situated in the Dorsoduro district and overlooking the Grand Canal next to Ca' Foscari. It is among the best examples of the late Venetian Gothic, and it was the final residence of Princess Louise of Artois.","wpu":"Palazzo Giustinian (Dorsoduro)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%28Venice%29_Palazzo_Giustinian.jpg/960px-%28Venice%29_Palazzo_Giustinian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ponte dei Tre Archi","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.44557,"lo":12.32072,"d":890,"ds":"The Ponte dei Tre Archi (Italian for \"Three Arches' Bridge\") is one of the main bridges of Venice, Italy, along with the Ponte delle Guglie, the other bridge spanning the Cannaregio Canal, and the four bridges spanning the Canal Grande: Rialto, Scalzi, Accademia, and the Costituzione.","wpu":"Ponte dei Tre Archi","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Ponte_dei_Tre_Archi_%28Venice%29.jpg/960px-Ponte_dei_Tre_Archi_%28Venice%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Le Eremite","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.4319,"lo":12.3245,"d":895,"ds":"Le Eremite is a small Catholic church in the Dorsoduro area of Venice, Italy. It was built at the end of the 17th century for Augustinian nuns. It formed part of a larger complex which included a convent and schools run by the nuns.","wpu":"Le Eremite","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Chiesa_delle_Eremite_-_Venezia.jpg/960px-Chiesa_delle_Eremite_-_Venezia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ognissanti, Venice","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.431131,"lo":12.3233,"d":908,"ds":"Ognissanti (Italian: Chiesa di Ognissanti) is a 16th-century Roman Catholic church located in the Dorsoduro sestiere of the Italian city of Venice.","wpu":"Ognissanti, Venice","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Chiesa_di_Ognissanti_-_Venezia.jpg/960px-Chiesa_di_Ognissanti_-_Venezia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tronchetto","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.440556,"lo":12.305,"d":978,"ds":"Tronchetto (also known as Isola nuova, meaning \"New island\") is an artificial island in the Venetian Lagoon, northern Italy, located at the westernmost tip of the main Venice island. The island was created in the 1960s, and now is used as a car park for tourists, since vehicles cannot be driven into the city historic center.","wpu":"Tronchetto","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a7/Tronchetto.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Santa Maria delle Penitenti","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.44671,"lo":12.31927,"d":984,"ds":"The church of Santa Maria delle Penitenti, is part of a large complex: Pio Loco delle Penitenti, located on the canal Cannaregio, near its exit to the lagoon facing Mestre, in the Northwest edge of Venice, Italy. It gained its name as a charitable institution providing an alternative life to former prostitutes, akin to a Magdalene asylum.","wpu":"Santa Maria delle Penitenti","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Santa_Maria_delle_Penitenti_%28Venice%29.jpg/960px-Santa_Maria_delle_Penitenti_%28Venice%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Samuele, Venice","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":45.433611,"lo":12.328056,"d":991,"ds":"San Samuele is a church in Venice, northern Italy. It is located in the eponymous campo near Palazzo Grassi and Palazzo Malipiero. The facade is set back on the campo, but faces and is visible from the Grand Canal.","wpu":"San Samuele, Venice","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Chiesa_di_San_Samuele.jpg/960px-Chiesa_di_San_Samuele.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Venice is a coastal city in northeastern Italy and the capital of the region of Veneto, as well as the Metropolitan City of Venice. It is built on a group of 126 islands that are separated by expanses of open water and by canals; portions of the city are linked by 472 bridges. The islands are in the shallow Venetian Lagoon, an enclosed bay lying between the mouths of the Po and the Piave rivers (more exactly between the Brenta and the Sile).","wpu":"Venice","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Venezia_aerial_view.jpg/960px-Venezia_aerial_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}